

r17-5664 restricted the negated FMA folds in match.pd to
!HONOR_SIGNED_ZEROS.  These tests expect those folds to apply with the
default options, so they started failing on aarch64.  Add
-fno-signed-zeros to them, as that commit did for the i386 FMA tests.

	PR middle-end/124820

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.dg/fma-5.c: Add -fno-signed-zeros.
	* gcc.dg/fma-6.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.dg/fma-7.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_cond_fnmla_1.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_cond_fnmla_2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_cond_fnmls_1.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_cond_fnmls_2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_fnmla_1.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_fnmla_2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_fnmls_1.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/unpacked_fnmls_2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/vcond_13.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/vcond_14.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/vcond_15.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/sve/vcond_16.c: Likewise.
---
 These are the 65 aarch64 failures reported by the Linaro CI after
 r17-5664.  Tested with an aarch64-linux-gnu cross compiler (they are
 all compile-only tests): all of them fail before this patch and pass
 after it.  Also checked gcc.dg/fma-[567].c on x86_64-pc-linux-gnu.

 The unpacked_cond_* and vcond_* tests cover the IFN_COND_* folds the
 original patch changed, so those changes are tested after all.

 My write access request is still pending, so I'd be grateful if
 someone could commit this once approved.

